      },
      "lengthKm": 5.793,
      "corners": 11,
      "firstHeld": 1922,
      "overview": "The Temple of Speed. Opened in 1922 inside a royal park, Monza is defined by enormous straights broken up by heavy braking zones, and it consistently produces the highest average speeds of the season. Teams run their skinniest rear wings of the year here.",
      "facts": [
        "Monza is one of the oldest purpose-built motor racing circuits in the world, opened in 1922.",
        "It sits inside the grounds of a former royal park on the edge of Monza, north of Milan.",
        "The abandoned banked oval from the old combined layout still stands on the site.",
        "Cars run their lowest-downforce set-ups of the season here in pursuit of straight-line speed."
      ],
