      },
      "lengthKm": 7.004,
      "corners": 19,
      "firstHeld": 1921,
      "overview": "The longest circuit on the Formula 1 calendar, cut through the forests of the Ardennes. Spa climbs and plunges through dramatic elevation changes, and its weather is famously local - one end of the lap can be soaked while the other stays dry.",
      "facts": [
        "Eau Rouge and the Raidillon climb that follows it are among the most celebrated corners in motorsport.",
        "The original 1920s layout ran for over 14 km on public roads between villages.",
        "The circuit was shortened to roughly its current configuration in 1979.",
        "Spa's micro-climate means it can rain on one section of the lap while another stays completely dry."
      ]
    },
