      "lengthKm": 13.626,
      "firstHeld": 1923,
      "overview": "Home of the 24 Hours of Le Mans since 1923, the Circuit de la Sarthe is part permanent circuit and part public road. Cars spend a huge proportion of the lap at full throttle, and crews have to balance outright speed against surviving a full day and night of racing.",
      "facts": [
        "The first 24 Hours of Le Mans was held in 1923, making it one of the oldest endurance races in the world.",
        "Much of the lap runs on public roads that are open to normal traffic for most of the year.",
        "Two chicanes were added to the Mulsanne Straight in 1990 to break up a run of nearly six kilometres.",
        "The race runs through the night, so drivers tackle the fastest sections in complete darkness."
      ],
